# code.gs contracts

Match the existing `var` / `function` style. Sheet names are exact: `scheme_codes`, `nav_data`.

## Entry points — do not rename
`onOpen` menu **Mutual Fund Matrix**; `showSidebar`; `showDialog` (1250×820); `doGet` (viewport meta); `getFundMatrixData(params)`.

## NAV
`loadNavIndex` reads `nav_data` once per call and keeps only scheme codes listed on `scheme_codes`. Match by `scheme_code`, not by fund name. `lookupNav` is the last NAV on or before the day. Do not synthesize NAV. Do not cache the sheet in `CacheService`.

## Params
`sipAmount` (1000), `sipDay` (5), `fromDate` (today minus 1 year), `toDate` (today), `saleDate` (today). Dates are `yyyy-MM-dd`.

Custom range: one SIP on `sipDay` each month from From through To, redeemed at the To Date NAV. Fields: `customRangeXirr`, `sipCorpus`, `netProfit`, `absoluteReturn`, `navStart`, `navEnd`, `units`, `investedAmount`. `redeem` splits that SIP into lots held 12 months or more (`ltcgGain`) and younger lots (`stcgGain`, plus `exitLoad` at 1% of those lots' value). `switchPath` is 36 month-end 3-year CAGRs ending on Sale Date, aligned with `pathMonths`. `saleNav` is the Sale Date NAV and is not an input to the custom range.

## Tenures (`TENURE_CONFIG`)
Calendar lookbacks from Sale Date, not fixed day counts. Short: `5D` `15D` `1M` `3M` `6M` `9M` `1Y`. Long: `2Y` `3Y` `5Y` `7Y` `10Y` `12Y`. `7Y` is intentional.
`tenureXirr` is an annualized Newton XIRR on a 365.25-day year, including 1M–9M. That is why those cells read higher than the period's price change. It is `null` when the fund has no NAV on or before the window start, or when the window has no SIP date. `5D` and `15D` are always null for XIRR. Do not relabel a shorter history as a full tenure.
`tenureCagr` is the point-to-point NAV change. Under 1Y it is absolute. From 1Y it is annualized with 365.25. It can be present when XIRR is null.
Keep this order identical to the client `TENURES` array.

## Risk (`fund.risk`)
Three years of daily NAV ending on Sale Date. Cash rate `0.065`. `volatility` is annualized standard deviation. Also `downsideDeviation`, `sharpe`, `sortino`, `treynor`, `maxDrawdown`, `maxDrawup`, `bestMonth`, `worstMonth`, `var95` (5th percentile of daily returns), `rollingReturn`, and `rollingHit` (share of monthly 1-year windows that were positive, over about four years). `upsideCapture`, `downsideCapture`, `beta`, `alpha`, `informationRatio`, `rSquared`, `correlation`, `trackingError`, and `trackingDifference` use the other tracked funds in the same category, not an index. Expense ratio stays on `getFundPublishedProfile` and is null when that call fails. Do not invent published fields.
